  "description": "The ordering proof for UPDATE-USER-INFO's five-arm EVALUATE TRUE at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:179-213. Two arms would match this input: the user id is blank AND the first name is blank. EVALUATE is ordered and the first matching WHEN wins, so the message must be 'User ID can NOT be empty...' from the arm at :180 and the cursor must be on USRIDINL - not 'First Name can NOT be empty...' and not FNAMEL. A translation that used an unordered structure, or that collected all the failures and reported the last, would produce the wrong message here while still reporting an error, and only an ordered expectation catches that.\n\nThe last name and password are deliberately populated, so the only reason those arms are not taken is that an earlier one was. The blanks are SPACES; case05 and case07 drive the same condition with LOW-VALUES.",
